cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "KazRNA-Pipe: a reproducible Nextflow workflow for integrated bulk and single-cell transcriptomic profiling"
abstract: >-
  A containerised Nextflow workflow combining three-way bulk RNA-seq
  quantification (STAR, HISAT2, Salmon), three-way differential expression
  (DESeq2, edgeR, limma-voom), CPU and GPU single-cell processing paths, and
  cross-method cell-type deconvolution. Every process runs in a container
  pinned by immutable digest, per-run provenance is recorded, and continuous
  integration verifies end-to-end execution under both Docker and Apptainer
  together with run-to-run determinism.
